THE WHOLE RESET IS ABOUT. The reset's concern is work that silently stops; this is work that silently RESTARTS, and both come from the same root -- the register's state is maintained by hand, by whoever remembers, and nothing ties a row's state to the PR that changed it. A row stuck at `queued` past its fix costs a duplicate dispatch; the same gap in the other direction is a row marked `done` that nobody did. [!] THE CHECKLIST HAS NO `prs` DISCIPLINE EITHER: E10's `prs` array was empty although #12676 carried its fix, so even a reader who doubted the state had nothing to follow. [!] CANDIDATE FIX, not prescribed: a guard that fails when a merged PR's body or commits name a checklist id whose row is still `queued`. That is checkable from git alone and needs no new register."}
{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 7, "clears_when": "`python3 scripts/ops/render_daily_brief.py | wc -c` returns a size a person will actually read — measured, with the threshold stated in the fix rather than left to taste — AND section 0 still names every due item, so the shrink came from field discipline or an honest, counted truncation rather than from dropping rows. Verified by RUNNING it against a store that has A8's ~1,150 items in it, not against today's 10.", "kind": "observation"}, "id": "PI-20260921-M07", "loud": true, "next_action": "dispatch_lane", "origin": {"kind": "session", "ref": "session_01XQhayAHWdrSYv8jN54P2HH (manager, 2026-09-21) — first real render of the merged brief", "rerun": "python3 scripts/ops/render_daily_brief.py | wc -c; # FINDING STILL APPLIES above roughly 12000 characters, or whenever section 0's longest row exceeds a few lines"}, "state": "queued", "what": "THE DAILY BRIEF RENDERS AT 42 KB / 140 LINES AND IS THEREFORE UNREADABLE, AND THE MANAGER CAUSED IT. MEASURED 2026-09-21 on the first real render after A3a merged (9751e17): 42,159 characters, of which section 0 is the bulk. The GENERATOR is not at fault — it renders each pipeline item's `what` and `routed_to` verbatim, which is correct behaviour for a store whose fields are sentences. The fault is upstream: this manager wrote paragraph-length `routed_to` essays (one is 90+ words) and multi-hundred-word `what` fields, and section 0 prints them in full. [!] THIS IS A NEAR MISS OF THE EXACT FAILURE A8 WAS WARNED AGAINST. A8's acceptance test was that section 0 must not become a wall of undispositioned rows, and it passed — zero of its 607 promoted rows flood it. Mine is a wall of DISPOSITIONED rows, which is better in kind and identical in effect: an operator who will not read it gets the same nothing either way, and the whole mechanism rests on them reading it daily. [!] IT GETS WORSE, NOT BETTER, ON ITS OWN: A8's import takes the store to ~1,150 items and 87 currently-due, against the 7 rendered here. [!] TWO CANDIDATE FIXES AND THEY ARE NOT EQUIVALENT, so do not just pick one: (a) the brief TRUNCATES per-row text with the full text one click away — cheap, but this repo's rule is that a truncation must never be able to hide, so it needs the count printed beside it; (b) the STORE gets a length discipline — `what` is one sentence, the reasoning lives in the linked artifact. (b) is the real fix and (a) is the mitigation. Prefer (b), and note the validator currently enforces a minimum on these fields and no maximum."}
