{"due_when": {"check_every_days": 3, "clears_when": "NO hook in .claude/settings.json INSTRUCTS a session to read, write, register in, or file into an archived path or retired skill. ⚠️ CORRECTED 2026-09-21 AND THE CORRECTION MATTERS: the original criterion said the mention-counting grep must print NOTHING, and a CORRECT fix cannot satisfy that — the repaired hooks deliberately NAME the archived files in sentences saying they are archived and must not be used, because a session needs the name it would otherwise go hunting for. Measured after the fix: 22 mentions -> 8, and all 8 are warnings. A criterion that would have forced me to strip those warnings to go green was a criterion pushing toward a WORSE artifact, which is the thing a pre-registered rule is supposed to prevent, not cause. Verify by READING the rendered session-start text, not by counting matches.", "kind": "observation"}, "id": "PI-20260921-M05", "loud": true, "next_action": "ask_operator", "origin": {"kind": "audit", "ref": "docs/audits/archived-register-readers-fable-probe.md (E11 Fable probe, merged #12681); re-counted independently by session_01XQhayAHWdrSYv8jN54P2HH before filing", "rerun": "grep -oE '(board-pointer|session-board|OPEN-ITEMS|health-review-backlog|performance-review-backlog|ml-review-backlog|research-review-backlog|system-review|delegate-work|MANAGER-LEASE|SESSIONS\\.json|duty)' .claude/settings.json | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn; # FINDING STILL APPLIES while this prints any line. Expected clear state: no output."}, "routed_to": "THE OPERATOR, via section 2 of the next daily brief. Not delegable: .claude/ is harness configuration, an agent editing it is refused [Self-Modification], and that refusal is correct and was not worked around. What is needed is either the operator making the edit or an explicit grant naming .claude/settings.json, the way the spawn-provenance grant named manager/SKILL.md.", "state": "done", "terminal_reason": "FIXED 2026-09-21 under operator grant (manager-s